tation\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/konard/konard.github.io/pull/14\"},{\"mergedAt\":\"2026-10-22T21:18:31Z\",\"number\":12,\"title\":\"Experience synced with hh.ru; a CV per position in EN/RU with 4 PDF styles; light/dark themes and 9 new positions\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/konard/konard.github.io/pull/12\"},{\"mergedAt\":\"2026-10-21T15:43:37Z\",\"number\":10,\"title\":\"Link networks with the zero link on the grid, problem solving diagram fixes, network gallery in Research, cleaner ecosystem\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/konard/konard.github.io/pull/10\"},{\"mergedAt\":\"2026-10-20T21:09:07Z\",\"number\":8,\"title\":\"Repositories by field and profession, role-filtered experience, research, associative stack, art, blog archive and links matrix rain\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/konard/konard.github.io/pull/8\"},{\"mergedAt\":\"2026-10-17T14:58:32Z\",\"number\":6,\"title\":\"Deploy to GitHub Pages with actions/deploy-pages and verify the live site\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/konard/konard.github.io/pull/6\"},{\"mergedAt\":\"2026-10-17T11:45:07Z\",\"number\":4,\"title\":\"Fix CI/CD warnings, false negatives and vulnerabilities (CRA → Vite, template best practices)\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/konard/konard.github.io/pull/4\"}]\n{\"body\":\"<img width=\\\"1824\\\" height=\\\"1112\\\" alt=\\\"Image\\\" src=\\\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/f66bbe69-110b-4e21-8d31-7899b6ac9bc4\\\" />\\n\\nhttps://konard.github.io/network/?code=2222&rotation=90&turns=15+-15&gaps=0.18+0.18+%7E+%7E&lang=en\\n\\nIf I use auto mode and omit angles I kind of works:\\n\\nhttps://konard.github.io/network/?code=2222&rotation=90&solve=true&gaps=0.18+0.18+%7E+%7E&lang=en\\n\\n<img width=\\\"1824\\\" height=\\\"1112\\\" alt=\\\"Image\\\" src=\\\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/830ce295-eb47-4d79-9c96-9f61f33e19de\\\" />\\n\\nBut if I removed gaps settings which were set manually it does not work:\\n\\n<img width=\\\"1824\\\" height=\\\"1112\\\" alt=\\\"Image\\\" src=\\\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/762dce8e-098c-4267-aa90-e532801768fd\\\" />\\n\\nIt should have been searching for gap configuration which reduces overlap, and also finds nearest configuration to specific padding/margin between all drawn shapes/paths and so on.\\n\\nSo `https://konard.github.io/network/?code=2222&rotation=90&turns=15+-15&gaps=0.18+0.18+%7E+%7E&lang=en` can be added as test case of perfect arrangement.\\n\\nYet it may be done even perfect, if the arrow is sharp (not rounded) - this also should be configurable if not yet.\\n\\nWe should make nice per link configuration editor, so it is easy to edit each configuration for each link, and we should use list of cards for each links where we put all inputs, so no expandable section is needed for per link configuration.\\n\\nAlso if angle of arrow is too small it stops being pointy, and becomes rounded that is a bug.\\n\\nAlso we should be able to make by default pointy arrow, that makes the line shorter, so both start and end of top link in the example would land on the same line in this configuration. At the moment the right pointy arrow is a little bit longer or closer to other bottom link. Yet for both gap is 0.18 and 0.18, which is not correct.\\n\\nThat behavior should be optional (disablable by default), to be able to keep backwards compatibility if needed, by by default we should make sure if the arrow is pointy we do line little bit shorter, so if we compare start and end of the link in length from middle to start/end their length is the same and `0.18 and 0.18` with same angles will land them on exactly the same horizontal line in this case.\\n\\nWe need to download all logs and data related about the issue to this repository, make sure we compile that data to `./docs/case-studies/issue-{id}` folder, and use it to do deep case study analysis (also make sure to search online for additional facts and data), in which we will reconstruct timeline/sequence of events, list of each and all requirements from the issue, find root causes of the each problem, and propose possible solutions and solution plans for each requirement (we should also check known existing components/libraries, that solve similar problem or can help in solutions).\\n\\nIf there is not enough data to find actual root cause, add debug output and verbose mode if not present, that will allow us to find root cause on next iteration.\\n\\nIf issue related to any other repository/project, where we can report issues on GitHub, please do so. Each issue must contain reproducible examples, workarounds and suggestions for fix the issue in code. Also double check to fully apply requirements to entire codebase, so if we have issue in multiple places, it should be fixed in all them.\\n\\nPlease plan and execute everything in this single pull request, you have unlimited time and context, as context auto-compacts and you can continue indefinitely, until it is each and every requirement fully addressed, and everything is totally done.\",\"comments\":[],\"title\":\"Improvements and fixes\"}\n{\"body\":\"Fixes #25\\n\\nAutomatic spacing now discovers gaps for `2222` without manual setup and measures the painted shafts and markers, including stroke width and configurable clearance. Sharp arrows keep acute tips and balance their painted endpoints by default; rounded, bevelled and inherited corners and legacy lengths remain selectable. Each link now has a responsive card containing all nine existing inputs, with visible gap overrides.\\n\\nThe shared geometry serves the preview, solver, SVG and raster exports. Gallery/rain defaults and existing link actions are preserved. Optional solver diagnostics default off. The bounded search remains heuristic: unattainable clearance within the configured bounds retains its residual score.\\n\\n### Reproduction and verification\\n\\n- Original failure: open `/network/?code=2222&rotation=90&solve=true&lang=en`. The original drawing collapses near the referenced middle. Automatic mode now finds both reference gaps and reduces the fixture's painted score from about 7.4386 to 0.\\n- Reference arrangement: `/network/?code=2222&rotation=90&turns=15+-15&gaps=0.18+0.18+%7E+%7E&lang=en`. Equal gaps now produce balanced painted extents. The same fixture at `endAngle=5` keeps its sharp tip.\\n- `node experiments/issue-25-reproduce.mjs` runs the new tests against the original source and restores current files: all six issue regressions fail as expected. A seventh regression protects the zero-gap fallback discovered during implementation.\\n- 717 unit tests; ESLint, formatting, file limits, secret scan, dependency audit, production build and all 120 CV PDFs.\\n- Native Chromium, Firefox and WebKit checks cover sharp endpoints at 5°/15°/45°, exact Apply/share/reload SVG equality, card editing/removal and English/Russian mobile layout. The raster check supersamples acute tips while retaining the same normalized tolerance.\\n- Existing editor/download, issue 19, issue 21 and issue 23 suites remain in the three-engine CI matrix, including the full 4131-card gallery and actual compositor checks. Local compatibility checks run sequentially within the container budget.\\n\\n[Detailed case study, requirement map, chronology, research and alternatives](https://github.com/konard/konard.github.io/blob/issue-25-665823cdf9ad/docs/case-studies/issue-25/README.md), [validation and archived logs/data](https://github.com/konard/konard.github.io/blob/issue-25-665823cdf9ad/docs/case-studies/issue-25/VALIDATION.md).\\n\\nFinal CI [40404466882](https://github.com/konard/konard.github.io/actions/runs/40404466882) passed for `09160c7099d84858dbc19a301451b9d2d4337c1c` (created 2026-10-26 21:27:10 UTC): all checks, 717 tests, five browser suites in each of Chromium/Firefox/macOS WebKit, the production build and all 120 CV PDFs. The complete logs and browser evidence from source run [40401691502](https://github.com/konard/konard.github.io/actions/runs/40401691502) are archived in the case study. Final review confirmed that `main` is an ancestor, there are no outstanding issue/PR comments, and the working tree is clean.\\n\\n### Visual evidence\\n\\nAutomatic mode, before and after:\\n\\n| Before | After |\\n| --- | --- |\\n| ![Before: collapsed automatic drawing](https://github.com/konard/konard.github.io/blob/issue-25-665823cdf9ad/docs/case-studies/issue-25/screenshots/before-auto.png?raw=true) | ![After: automatically spaced painted shapes](https://github.com/konard/konard.github.io/blob/issue-25-665823cdf9ad/docs/case-studies/issue-25/screenshots/chromium-after-auto.png?raw=true) |\\n\\nBalanced endpoints and acute tips:\\n\\n| Before | After |\\n| --- | --- |\\n| ![Before: unequal manual endpoints](https://github.com/konard/konard.github.io/blob/issue-25-665823cdf9ad/docs/case-studies/issue-25/screenshots/before-manual.png?raw=true) | ![After: balanced sharp endpoints](https://github.com/konard/konard.github.io/blob/issue-25-665823cdf9ad/docs/case-studies/issue-25/screenshots/chromium-after-manual.png?raw=true) |\\n| ![Before: acute tip is lost](https://github.com/konard/konard.github.io/blob/issue-25-665823cdf9ad/docs/case-studies/issue-25/screenshots/before-acute.png?raw=true) | ![After: acute tip remains sharp](https://github.com/konard/konard.github.io/blob/issue-25-665823cdf9ad/docs/case-studies/issue-25/screenshots/chromium-after-acute.png?raw=true) |\\n\\nPer-link controls, before and after:\\n\\n| Before | After |\\n| --- | --- |\\n| ![Before: table and separate gap disclosure](https://github.com/konard/konard.github.io/blob/issue-25-665823cdf9ad/docs/case-studies/issue-25/screenshots/before-editor.png?raw=true) | ![After: cards with every link input](https://github.com/konard/konard.github.io/blob/issue-25-665823cdf9ad/docs/case-studies/issue-25/screenshots/chromium-after-editor.png?raw=true) |\\n\",\"comments\":[{\"id\":\"IC_kwDON1sLX88AAAABfyHP5A\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"konard\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"<!-- hive-mind:working-session-summary -->\\n## Working session summary\\n\\nImplemented issue #25 in [PR #26](https://github.com/konard/konard.github.io/pull/26), now ready for review.\\n\\n- Improved automatic spacing, sharp balanced arrows, and per-link editing cards.\\n- Added regression tests, before/after screenshots, and a detailed case study.\\n- Verified 717 tests, three browser engines, production build, 120 CV PDFs, and all CI checks.\\n\\nWorking tree is clean. PR remains unmerged.\\n\\n---\\n*This summary was automatically extracted from the AI working session output.*\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-26T21:34:47Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/konard/konard.github.io/pull/26#issuecomment-6427889636\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":true},{\"id\":\"IC_kwDON1sLX88AAAABfyHjsQ\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"konard\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"## 🤖 Solution Draft Log\\nThis log file contains the complete execution trace of the AI solution draft process.\\n\\n### 💰 **Cost estimation:**\\n- Model: GPT-6.1 Sol\\n- Provider: OpenAI\\n- Public pricing estimate: $6.075064\\n\\n### 📊 **Context and tokens usage:**\\n- 583.4K input tokens across requests (cumulative, larger than the 272K context window, so not one request's context), 80.9K / 128K (63%) output tokens\\n\\nTotal: (583.4K + 12.6M cached) input tokens, 80.9K output tokens, $6.075064 cost\\n\\n### 🤖 **Models used:**\\n- Tool: OpenAI Codex\\n- Requested: `gpt-6.1-sol`\\n- Thinking level: xhigh (~31999 tokens)\\n- **Model: GPT-6.1 Sol** (`gpt-6.1-sol`)\\n\\n### 📎 **Log file uploaded as Gist** (2564KB)\\n- [View complete solution draft log](https://gist.githubusercontent.com/konard/b96316e630d48921dfdf4e6145ba885e/raw/40b15884521d27e0b8a244cf2cfbede8f42e8cc7/tmp-hive-mind-log-upload-wGyvZj-sanitized.log.txt)\\n\\n---\\n*Now working session is ended, feel free to review and add any feedback on