[2026-10-27T20:04:29.404Z] [STDOUT] {"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_72","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc 'cat docs/case-studies/issue-27/data/issue-27.json; cat src/links/issue-27.test.js; cat src/pages/network-27.test.jsx; cat src/workflow.test.js; cat .prettierignore'","aggregated_output":"{\"body\":\"<img width=\\\"1824\\\" height=\\\"1112\\\" alt=\\\"Image\\\" src=\\\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/cd7dc1bf-19db-4cd5-a334-4bbc9b25bb60\\\" />\\n<img width=\\\"1824\\\" height=\\\"1112\\\" alt=\\\"Image\\\" src=\\\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/07c18fb4-ce65-462b-bda6-6424dc0dfe15\\\" />\\n\\nThis is the link where I got it to the closest to perfect https://konard.github.io/network/?code=1111&rotation=-90&turns=0+0%2C-15+15&gaps=0.08+0.07+%7E+%7E%2C0.18+0.18+%7E+%7E Yet looks like 0.07 is still to close as a reference and 0.08 id too much of a gap. Rotation can be ignored for tests, and it works as expected. `turns=0+0%2C-15+15` that looks strange, do we not have 0 as defaults? Do we need to enter zerors? May be we can use some delimeter to just skip first item to make url shorter.\\n\\nAlso double check across our history of url changes and we do support all previous urls configuraton as I gave some public links to them, so backward compatibility must be preserved, and if we have a shorter version of the url it should be updated when user comes to the page (with write to history of browser).\\n\\nBy default `Gap at the target reference` results in much bigger gap on fully closed self referencing link, meaning 0.08 makes too much of a gap, yet 0.07 is closer to perfection, yet by default they must be exactly the same (must be tested and measured).\\n\\nSomething is wrong with switching between 0.07 and 0.08 of this setting, there is sudden jump, yet between 0.00 and 0.07 no such sudden jumps.\\n\\nAlso up/down buttons of this configurator should not reset the value to zero (i mean up/down should go in steps of 0.01, not 1, for some reason there is UI bug, I clicked on up or down and got zero instead of 0.07).\\n\\nAlso on all sliders and also input fields with numbers we need to double check keyboard arrows work, and double check for all other obvious and intuitive keyboard keys and short cuts are supported.\\n\\nAlso experiemental automatic gap in this case didn't end up at this configuration, may it is because we don't set preority to not break fully self closing ling by default. So if link is fully self closed most likely it is already at perfect position or partially closed (the closed part of it is already perfect). By default we should prioritize to changing gaps and angles in this experimental feature for other open ended links.\\n\\nAnd this exact perfect arrangement should be added to tests.\\n\\nLast time we did nice work at https://github.com/konard/konard.github.io/issues/25 on making 0.18 and 0.18 for upper link to land on exactly the same line, but the closed links was not perfected enough or broken.\\n\\nWe need to download all logs and data related about the issue to this repository, make sure we compile that data to `./docs/case-studies/issue-{id}` folder, and use it to do deep case study analysis (also make sure to search online for additional facts and data), in which we will reconstruct timeline/sequence of events, list of each and all requirements from the issue, find root causes of the each problem, and propose possible solutions and solution plans for each requirement (we should also check known existing components/libraries, that solve similar problem or can help in solutions).\\n\\nIf there is not enough data to find actual root cause, add debug output and verbose mode if not present, that will allow us to find root cause on next iteration.\\n\\nIf issue related to any other repository/project, where we can report issues on GitHub, please do so. Each issue must contain reproducible examples, workarounds and suggestions for fix the issue in code. Also double check to fully apply requirements to entire codebase, so if we have issue in multiple places, it should be fixed in all them.\\n\\nPlease plan and execute everything in this single pull request, you have unlimited time and context, as context auto-compacts and you can continue indefinitely, until it is each and every requirement fully addressed, and everything is totally done.\",\"comments\":[],\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-27T19:45:26Z\",\"number\":27,\"title\":\"Default gaps are still not perfect enough\",\"updatedAt\":\"2026-10-27T19:49:39Z\"}\nimport { expect, it } from 'vitest';\nimport { glyphCurves, paintedCurve } from './glyph';\nimport { overlapCost, solveCollisions } from './collisions';\nimport { normalizeStyle, shapeOfStyle, linkTurns, styleFromParams, styleToParams } from './style';\nimport { linkGaps } from './gaps';\n\nconst links = [\n  [1, 1],\n  [1, 1],\n];\nconst setup = (patch = {}) => shapeOfStyle(normalizeStyle({ rotation: -90, turns: '0 0,-15 15', ...patch }), 2);\nconst extent = (shape) => {\n  const raw = glyphCurves(links, shape)[0];\n  const paint = paintedCurve(raw, shape);\n  const extra = shape.strokeWidth / 2 / Math.sin((shape.endAngle * Math.PI) / 180);\n  const apex = paint.end.at.map((v, i) => v + extra * paint.end.dir[i]);\n  const radius = (p) => Math.hypot(...p.map((v, i) => v - raw.middle.at[i]));\n  return { source: radius(raw.start.at) - shape.strokeWidth / 2, target: radius(apex) };\n};\nit('measures exactly equal painted gaps at both ends of the closed 1111 link', () => {\n  for (const rotation of [-90, 0, 45, 90])\n    for (const endAngle of [5, 15, 45, 85]) {\n      const measured = extent(setup({ rotation, endAngle }));\n      expect(measured.target).toBeCloseTo(measured.source, 9);\n    }\n});\nit('changes the target gap continuously through 0.07 and 0.08 without moving the source gap', () => {\n  const samples = [0.06, 0.07, 0.079, 0.08, 0.081, 0.09].map((gap) =>\n    extent(setup({ gaps: `0.08 ${gap} ~ ~,0.18 0.18 ~ ~` })),\n  );\n  for (let i = 1; i < samples.length; i++) {\n    expect(samples[i].source).toBeCloseTo(samples[0].source, 9);\n    const step = [0.01, 0.009, 0.001, 0.001, 0.009][i - 1];\n    expect(samples[i].target - samples[i - 1].target).toBeCloseTo(step * 60, 8);\n  }\n});\nit('preserves closed halves and discovers gaps and turns on the open 1111 link', () => {\n  const shape = shapeOfStyle(normalizeStyle({ rotation: -90 }), 2);\n  const result = solveCollisions(links, shape, { adjustGaps: true });\n  expect(result.turns[0]).toEqual([0, 0]);\n  expect(result.linkGaps[0]).toEqual(shape.linkGaps[0]);\n  expect(result.linkGaps[1][0]).toBeGreaterThan(0.08);\n  expect(result.linkGaps[1][1]).toBeGreaterThan(0.08);\n  expect(result.after).toBeLessThan(result.before);\n  expect(overlapCost(links, { ...shape, turns: result.turns, linkGaps: result.linkGaps })).toBeCloseTo(result.after, 8);\n});\nit('recognizes the exact reported arrangement with the closed gaps corrected to equality', () => {\n  const shape = setup({ gaps: '0.08 0.08 ~ ~,0.18 0.18 ~ ~' });\n  expect(overlapCost(links, shape)).toBeCloseTo(30 * 0.002, 8);\n  const result = solveCollisions(links, shape, { adjustGaps: true });\n  expect(result.turns[0]).toEqual([0, 0]);\n  expect(result.linkGaps[0]).toEqual([0.08, 0.08, null, null]);\n});\nit('preserves the closed side and its middle cut on a partially self-referencing link', () => {\n  const partial = [\n    [1, 2],\n    [1, 1],\n  ];\n  const shape = setup({ turns: '15 0', gaps: '0.09 ~ 1 ~' });\n  const result = solveCollisions(partial, shape, { adjustGaps: true });\n  expect(result.turns[0][0]).toBe(15);\n  expect(result.linkGaps[0][0]).toBe(0.09);\n  expect(result.linkGaps[0][2]).toBe(1);\n});\nit('accepts old turn/gap rows and serializes skipped defaults compactly', () => {\n  const old = styleFromParams(new URLSearchParams('turns=0+0%2C-15+15&gaps=~+~+~+~%2C0.18+0.18+~+~'));\n  const compact = styleToParams(old);\n  expect(compact.get('turns')).toBe(',-15 15');\n  expect(compact.get('gaps')).toBe(',0.18 0.18');\n  const next = styleFromParams(compact);\n  expect(linkTurns(next, 2)).toEqual([\n    [0, 0],\n    [-15, 15],\n  ]);\n  expect(linkGaps(next, 2)).toEqual([\n    [null, null, null, null],\n    [0.18, 0.18, null, null],\n  ]);\n  expect(styleFromParams(styleToParams(next))).toEqual(next);\n});\nimport { act, fireEvent, render, screen } from '@testing-library/react';\nimport { afterEach, expect, it, vi } from 'vitest';\nimport NetworkPage from './NetworkPage';\n\nafterEach(() => {\n  vi.useRealTimers();\n  window.history.replaceState(null, '', '/');\n});\nconst open = () => {\n  window.history.replaceState(\n    null,\n    '',\n    '/network/?code=1111&lang=en&turns=0+0%2C-15+15&gaps=~+~+~+~%2C0.18+0.18+~+~#links',\n  );\n  render(<NetworkPage />);\n};\nit('upgrades an old URL in browser history while preserving its drawing, language and anchor', () => {\n  vi.useFakeTimers();\n  open();\n  const drawing = document.querySelector('.network__preview').innerHTML;\n  const replace = vi.spyOn(window.history, 'replaceState');\n  act(() => vi.advanceTimersByTime(450));\n  const params = new URLSearchParams(window.location.search);\n  expect(params.get('turns')).toBe(',-15 15');\n  expect(params.get('gaps')).toBe(',0.18 0.18');\n  expect(params.get('lang')).toBe('en');\n  expect(window.location.hash).toBe('#links');\n  expect(replace).toHaveBeenCalledTimes(1);\n  expect(document.querySelector('.network__preview').innerHTML).toBe(drawing);\n  replace.mockRestore();\n});\nit('steps inherited gaps from the displayed global value, with decimal precision', () => {\n  open();\n  const input = screen.getByLabelText('Link 1: Gap at the target reference');\n  expect(input).toHaveValue(null);\n  fireEvent.keyDown(input, { key: 'ArrowUp' });\n  expect(input).toHaveValue(0.09);\n  fireEvent.keyDown(input, { key: 'ArrowDown' });\n  expect(input).toHaveValue(0.08);\n  fireEvent.keyDown(input, { key: 'PageDown' });\n  expect(input).toHaveValue(0);\n});\nit('supports page steps on every range while preserving modified editing shortcuts', () => {\n  open();\n  const input = screen.getByLabelText('Gap at the target reference', { selector: 'input[type=\"range\"]' });\n  fireEvent.keyDown(input, { key: 'PageUp' });\n  expect(input).toHaveValue('0.18');\n  fireEvent.keyDown(input, { key: 'Home' });\n  expect(input).toHaveValue('0');\n  fireEvent.keyDown(input, { key: 'End' });\n  expect(input).toHaveValue('1');\n});\nit('allows clearing a turn while typing a replacement and retains text-navigation keys', () => {\n  open();\n  const input = screen.getByLabelText('Link 2: turn of the source, °');\n  fireEvent.change(input, { target: { value: '' } });\n  expect(input).toHaveValue(null);\n  fireEvent.change(input, { target: { value: '-25' } });\n  expect(input).toHaveValue(-25);\n  fireEvent.keyDown(input, { key: 'Home' });\n  expect(input).toHaveValue(-25);\n  fireEvent.keyDown(input, { key: 'a', ctrlKey: true });\n  expect(input).toHaveValue(-25);\n});\nimport fs from 'fs';\nimport path from 'path';\nimport yaml from 'js-yaml';\n\nconst workflowsDir = path.join(__dirname, '..', '.github', 'workflows');\n\ndescribe('GitHub Actions workflows', () => {\n  const files = fs.readdirSync(workflowsDir).filter((f) => /\\.ya?ml$/.test(f));\n\n  test.each(files)('%s is valid YAML with jobs', (file) => {\n    const doc = yaml.load(fs.readFileSync(path.join(workflowsDir, file), 'utf8'));\n    expect(doc).toHaveProperty('jobs');\n    Object.values(doc.jobs).forEach((job) => {\n      expect(Array.isArray(job.steps)).toBe(true);\n      job.steps.forEach((step) => expect(typeof (step.name || step.uses)).toBe('string'));\n    });\n  });\n\n  // Issue #5: GitHub Pages is set to deploy from GitHub Actions (\"build_type\": \"workflow\"),\n  // so a commit to docs/ never reaches the site. Only actions/deploy-pages publishes it.\n  describe('GitHub Pages deployment from Actions', () => {\n    const doc = yaml.load(fs.readFileSync(path.join(workflowsDir, 'github-pages.yml'), 'utf8'));\n    const { deploy, test: testJob } = doc.jobs;\n    const scripts = Object.values(doc.jobs)\n      .flatMap((job) => job.steps.map((s) => s.run || ''))\n      .join('\\n');\n\n    test('the tested build is uploaded as the Pages artifact', () => {\n      const upload = testJob.steps.find((s) => (s.uses || '').startsWith('actions/upload-pages-artifact@'));\n      expect(upload).toBeDefined();\n      expect(upload.with.path).toBe('build/');\n      const build = testJob.steps.findIndex((s) => s.run === 'npm run build');\n      expect(build).toBeGreaterThanOrEqual(0);\n      expect(testJob.steps.indexOf(upload)).toBeGreaterThan(build);\n    });\n\n    // Issue #11: the \"Download PDF\" links point at PDFs printed after the build.\n    test('the CV PDFs are printed into the build before it is uploaded', () => {\n      const index = (run) => testJob.steps.findIndex((s) => s.run === run);\n      const upload = testJob.steps.findIndex((s) => (s.uses || '').startsWith('actions/upload-pages-artifact@'));\n      expect(index('npx playwright install --with-deps chromium')).toBeGreaterThan(index('npm run build'));\n      expect(index('npm run build:cv')).toBeGreaterThan(index('npx playwright install --with-deps chromium'));\n      expect(upload).toBeGreaterThan(index('npm run build:cv'));\n    });\n\n    test('deploy publishes with actions/deploy-pages to the github-pages environment', () => {\n      expect(deploy.steps.some((s) => (s.uses || '').startsWith('actions/deploy-pages@'))).toBe(true);\n      expect(deploy.permissions).toEqual({ contents: 'read', pages: 'write', 'id-token': '[REDACTED]' });\n      expect(deploy.environment.name).toBe('github-pages');\n      expect(deploy.environment.url).toBe('${{ steps.deployment.outputs.page_url }}');\n    });\n\n    test('nothing commits the build to the repository any more', () => {\n      expect(scripts).not.toMatch(/git (commit|push)/);\n      expect(scripts).not.toMatch(/cp -r build/);\n      Object.values(doc.jobs).forEach((job) => expect((job.permissions || {}).contents).not.toBe('write'));\n    });\n\n    test('deploy fails unless the deployed URL serves the app', () => {\n      const deployStep = deploy.steps.findIndex((s) => s.id === 'deployment');\n      const verify = deploy.steps.findIndex((s) => (s.run || '').includes('scripts/check-deployed-site.sh'));\n      expect(verify).toBeGreaterThan(deployStep);\n      expect(deploy.steps[verify].env.PAGE_URL).toBe('${{ steps.deployment.outputs.page_url }}');\n      expect(fs.existsSync(path.join(__dirname, '..', 'scripts', 'check-deployed-site.sh'))).toBe(true);\n    });\n\n    test('docs/ holds no stale site build that looks deployed', () => {\n      const docsDir = path.join(__dirname, '..', 'docs');\n      expect(fs.readdirSync(docsDir).filter((f) => f !== 'case-studies')).toEqual([]);\n    });\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe('GitHub Actions best practices', () => {\n  const files = fs.readdirSync(workflowsDir).filter((f) => /\\.ya?ml$/.test(f));\n  const docs = files.map((file) => [file, yaml.load(fs.readFileSync(path.join(workflowsDir, file), 'utf8'))]);\n  const steps = (doc) => Object.values(doc.jobs).flatMap((job) => job.steps);\n\n  test.each(docs)('%s sets a timeout on every job', (_file, doc) => {\n    Object.values(doc.jobs).forEach((job) => expect(job['timeout-minutes']).toBeGreaterThan(0));\n  });\n\n  test.each(docs)('%s defaults to read-only permissions', (_file, doc) => {\n    expect(doc.permissions).toEqual({ contents: 'read' });\n  });\n\n  // Actions that still target the deprecated Node.js 20 runtime print a warning on every run.\n  test.each(docs)('%s uses actions that run on Node.js 24', (_file, doc) => {\n    const minimum = {\n      'actions/checkout': 6,\n      'actions/setup-node': 6,\n      'actions/upload-artifact': 7,\n      'actions/download-artifact': 8,\n      'actions/upload-pages-artifact': 5,\n      'actions/deploy-pages': 5,\n    };\n    steps(doc)\n      .filter((s) => s.uses && !s.uses.startsWith('docker://'))\n      .forEach((s) => {\n        const [name, ref] = s.uses.split('@');\n        if (minimum[name]) expect(Number(ref.replace(/^v/, ''))).toBeGreaterThanOrEqual(minimum[name]);\n      });\n  });\n\n  test.each(docs)('%s only keeps checkout credentials where it pushes', (_file, doc) => {\n    Object.values(doc.jobs).forEach((job) => {\n      const writes = job.permissions && job.permissions.contents === 'write';\n      job.steps\n        .filter((s) => (s.uses || '').startsWith('actions/checkout@'))\n        .forEach((s) => {\n          if (!writes) expect(s.with && s.with['persist-credentials']).toBe(false);\n        });\n    });\n  });\n\n  test('main deploys are never cancelled by a newer push', () => {\n    const doc = yaml.load(fs.readFileSync(path.join(workflowsDir, 'github-pages.yml'), 'utf8'));\n    expect(doc.concurrency['cancel-in-progress']).toBe(\"${{ github.event_name == 'pull_request' }}\");\n  });\n\n  test('deploy publishes the tested build instead of rebuilding it', () => {\n    const doc = yaml.load(fs.readFileSync(path.join(workflowsDir, 'github-pages.yml'), 'utf8'));\n    expect(doc.jobs.deploy.needs).toBe('test');\n    expect(doc.jobs.deploy.steps.some((s) => (s.run || '').includes('npm run build'))).toBe(false);\n    expect(doc.jobs.deploy.steps.some((s) => (s.uses || '').startsWith('actions/deploy-pages@'))).toBe(true);\n  });\n});\nbuild\ndocs\ndev\ncoverage\nnode_modules\npackage-lock.json\nsrc/data/github.json\nsrc/data/repositories.json\nsrc/data/habr.json\nsrc/data/posts.json\nsrc/skins.frames.css\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
