[2026-10-27T20:04:40.490Z] [STDOUT] {"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_76","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfor n in (18,20):\n p=json.load(open(f'docs/case-studies/issue-27/data/pr-{n}.json'))\n print('PR',n,p['body'])\nPY\nrg -n 'type=\\\"number\\\"|type=\\\"range\\\"' src\ncat docs/case-studies/issue-27/logs/url-history-audit.log\nsed -n '340,480p' src/links/style.js\nsed -n '235,300p' experiments/issue-27-browser.mjs\"","aggregated_output":"PR 18 Clicking a gallery card now opens `/network/?code=…` with that exact network. The page edits its notations and individual links, configures its SVG, and downloads or shares the resulting picture. The small share icon appears on hover or keyboard focus and opens the sharing section.\n\nFixes #17\n\n- Edit theory notation (L → L² or R → R²), pairs, the N-ary number, exact decimal index and links notation. Supports every gallery configuration and networks of 1–9 links, with add/remove, reference editing, previous/next, random and canonical renaming.\n- Configure endpoint angles and per-link turns; start/end/middle markers and sizes; curves, loops, spacing, margins and rotation; colours, line styles, opacity and glow; transparent/solid/gradient backgrounds; optional cards and border styles. Includes plain black without a card, presets, captions, image sizes and saved styles.\n- Download SVG, PNG, JPEG, WebP and `.lino`; copy the link, image or SVG; use native sharing where supported or ten social/email share links. The address preserves the complete picture, theory notation and explicit page language.\n- Opt into experimental overlap reduction by adjusting endpoint angles; inspect the score, apply the turns or clear them.\n\nRecovered the interrupted session requested in the PR comment. Reproduced and fixed its unfinished sticky-preview layout, partial notation parsing, inconsistent collision scoring/clamped applied turns, receiver-dependent theory captions and lost language parameters. Each correctness fix has a regression test; the layout has before/after screenshots and a browser visibility assertion.\n\nVerification:\n\n[CI passed on final commit `71d2a9b`](https://github.com/konard/konard.github.io/actions/runs/40115390362).\n\n- All 565 unit/data/workflow tests; lint, formatting, line limits, secret scan, production build and dependency audit (0 vulnerabilities).\n- Chromium browser checks are now part of CI: gallery navigation, editable notations/invalid input, styling, solver application, URL round trips in a fresh browser, actual downloaded file contents/dimensions/transparency, language reload and 360–1920 px layouts in EN/RU. The browser suite also passed in Firefox.\n- All 120 CV PDFs passed the existing page-count, text-layer and reading-order checks.\n- Bounded solver experiment: 507 of 720 three-link classes improved, 213 unchanged, none worse. Default gallery/rain SVGs match `main` byte for byte across 4,693 configurations.\n\nTo reproduce the original layout bug, open `/network/?code=221331` on desktop and scroll to Style: previously the preview was entirely above the viewport. It now stays beside the controls. Run `npm run build && npm run test:network:browser`; parser/solver/URL regressions are in `src/links/network.test.js` and `src/pages/network.test.jsx`.\n\n| Before | After |\n| --- | --- |\n| ![Preview out of view](https://github.com/konard/konard.github.io/blob/issue-17-c029b2b48293/docs/case-studies/issue-17/screenshots/before-style-preview.png?raw=true) | ![Sticky preview beside styles](https://github.com/konard/konard.github.io/blob/issue-17-c029b2b48293/docs/case-studies/issue-17/screenshots/after-style-preview.png?raw=true) |\n\n![Network editor](https://github.com/konard/konard.github.io/blob/issue-17-c029b2b48293/docs/case-studies/issue-17/screenshots/network-desktop.png?raw=true)\n\n| Plain black, no card | Experimental overlap reduction |\n| --- | --- |\n| ![Plain black](https://github.com/konard/konard.github.io/blob/issue-17-c029b2b48293/docs/case-studies/issue-17/screenshots/plain-black.png?raw=true) | ![Reduced overlaps](https://github.com/konard/konard.github.io/blob/issue-17-c029b2b48293/docs/case-studies/issue-17/screenshots/collisions-after.png?raw=true) |\n\n[Requirement-by-requirement evidence, mobile/light screenshots and reproducible experiments](https://github.com/konard/konard.github.io/blob/issue-17-c029b2b48293/docs/case-studies/issue-17/README.md).\n\nThe overlap solver is a heuristic and remains opt-in. Static social link previews are shared across networks; attach the downloaded/copied image or use native file sharing for the actual picture. Clipboard/native sharing depend on browser support. An optional WebKit run could not finish within the container's 2.92 GiB memory limit (browser lost on the gallery); no passing WebKit run is claimed.\n\nPR 20 Fixes #19\n\nSlider changes previously wrote to browser history on every input; Safari's quota exception could remove the editor. History now updates after release and 400 ms of quiet, with bounded retries and exception handling. Preview and share links update immediately. Other history-writing paths receive the same exception protection.\n\n- Fixed self-reference leaving/entering angles, curvature and bend. Hide controls that cannot affect the current network.\n- Added independent reference gaps and symmetric start/end/middle marker sizes, angles, tangent/sideways offsets and rotations. Optional cuts on either side of the middle support open rings; the default line stays continuous.\n- Applied the requested editor defaults with rotation still zero, while preserving gallery/rain geometry and the gallery preset.\n- Added square, hexagonal, dice, playing-card, sunflower and deterministic D3 force placement. Automatic placement uses a circle for 1–4 links. Removed the nine-link limit throughout notations, editing, colours, turns, URLs and exports; large indices/counts remain exact.\n- Fixed Safari image clipboard activation by passing a PNG promise to `ClipboardItem` during the click. Native sharing prepares images in advance and retains synchronous link sharing while preparation is pending. Unsupported clipboard capabilities expose download/selectable-link alternatives.\n- Corrected large-number fields overflowing their mobile panel and coalesced native-share image rendering during rapid edits.\n\n## Reproduction and tests\n\nThe retained [reproduction experiment](https://github.com/konard/konard.github.io/blob/issue-19-8244f16d7529/experiments/issue-19-reproduce.mjs) injects a bounded history quota and records the original blank screen. Failing tests were recorded before each correction; the [case study](https://github.com/konard/konard.github.io/blob/issue-19-8244f16d7529/docs/case-studies/issue-19/README.md) maps every issue requirement to implementation and evidence, including source data, primary-source research, alternatives and default-off diagnostics.\n\n- Unit coverage includes all 4,181 networks with 1–3 links, self-reference controls, marker symmetry, exact cubic cuts, interaction timing, clipboard/share activation, eight placement modes at eleven sizes, and all notation round trips at 10/37/100 links.\n- Browser regressions cover 120-event drags, repeated releases, injected history failure/recovery, both complete issue URLs, actual PNG clipboard writes, image downloads, seven distinct layouts, shared-URL reloads and a 100-link touch editor. Existing gallery/editor/export regressions run in Chromium, Firefox and WebKit in CI.\n- Local checks: ESLint, Prettier, file limits, secret scanning, all 682 unit tests, production build, all 120 CV PDFs and a dependency audit with zero vulnerabilities. Browser engines run sequentially locally; CI preserves screenshots and result JSON for each engine.\n\nFinal validation: [CI run 40131510761](https://github.com/konard/konard.github.io/actions/runs/40131510761) passes on the published head `49a22927e75bb29e1806a69c8f2c22ca25311853`: lint, repository checks, all three browser engines, 682 unit tests, production build, all 120 CV PDFs and the Pages artifact. Deployment is intentionally skipped for pull requests. The passing implementation run’s raw logs and browser artifacts are archived in the case study.\n\nTouch tests use browser emulation; operating-system share sheets use gesture-sensitive component tests. The case study records these verification limits. Linux WebKit r2370 has a confirmed upstream backdrop-filter regression ([Playwright #43426](https://github.com/microsoft/playwright/issues/43426), [WebKit 327850](https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=327850)); bounded probes reproduce it and verify the documented stable Playwright 1.63.0 pin with the unchanged glass gallery. Full browser suites remain enabled for all three engines; CI runs them on separate runners.\n\n## Before and after\n\nHistory quota: reproduced blank screen, then the editor surviving a rejected history write:\n\n![Before: blank editor](https://github.com/konard/konard.github.io/blob/issue-19-8244f16d7529/docs/case-studies/issue-19/screenshots/before-history-error.png?raw=true)\n![After: usable editor](https://github.com/konard/konard.github.io/blob/issue-19-8244f16d7529/docs/case-studies/issue-19/screenshots/chromium-after-history-error.png?raw=true)\n\nOptional ring cuts and independent marker offsets:\n\n![Ring cuts and markers](https://github.com/konard/konard.github.io/blob/issue-19-8244f16d7529/docs/case-studies/issue-19/screenshots/chromium-ring-and-offsets.png?raw=true)\n\nPhysical placement for 17 links:\n\n![Force placement](https://github.com/konard/konard.github.io/blob/issue-19-8244f16d7529/docs/case-studies/issue-19/screenshots/chromium-layout-force.png?raw=true)\n\nLarge-number mobile fields before and after:\n\n![Before: clipped fields](https://github.com/konard/konard.github.io/blob/issue-19-8244f16d7529/docs/case-studies/issue-19/screenshots/before-mobile-large.png?raw=true)\n![After: fields fit](https://github.com/konard/konard.github.io/blob/issue-19-8244f16d7529/docs/case-studies/issue-19/screenshots/chromium-mobile-100-links.png?raw=true)\n\nsrc/sound/interactions.js:74:        if (target?.matches?.('input[type=\"range\"]')) play('select', 70);\nsrc/sound/sound.test.jsx:301:    expect(clickEvent(element('<input type=\"range\">'))).toBe(null);\nsrc/sound/sound.test.jsx:321:      <input id=\"r\" type=\"range\"><input id=\"t\" type=\"text\"><select id=\"s\"><option>1</option></select>\nsrc/pages/network-27.test.jsx:45:  const input = screen.getByLabelText('Gap at the target reference', { selector: 'input[type=\"range\"]' });\nsrc/pages/SettingsPage.jsx:40:        type=\"range\"\nsrc/pages/useNetworkHistory.js:14:const continuous = (target) => target?.matches?.('input[type=\"range\"], input[type=\"color\"]');\nsrc/pages/NetworkStyle.jsx:45:        type=\"range\"\nsrc/components/NumberInput.jsx:17:      type=\"number\"\n(!) Your Vite config uses features that are unsupported by `configLoader: 'native'`, which is planned to become the default in a future major version of Vite:\n  - import \"./fields\" without a file extension (src/settings/schema.js:15:32). Add the file extension\n  - import \"./schema.background\" without a file extension (src/settings/schema.js:16:37). Add the file extension\n  - import \"./schema.layers\" without a file extension (src/settings/schema.js:17:32). Add the file extension\n  - import \"./schema.skins\" without a file extension (src/settings/schema.js:18:31). Add the file extension\n  - import \"./schema.sound\" without a file extension (src/settings/schema.js:19:31). Add the file extension\n  - import \"./schema.skins\" without a file extension (src/settings/schema.js:21:33). Add the file extension\n  - import \"./fields\" without a file extension (src/settings/schema.sound.js:7:47). Add the file extension\n  - import \"./fields\" without a file extension (src/settings/schema.background.js:3:54). Add t