)                        |\n| Issue 25 browser suite, Firefox                  | Pass                                                                                                                        | [log](logs/firefox-browser.log), [JSON](data/firefox-browser.json)                                         |\n| Issue 25 browser suite, WebKit                   | Pass, including Linux-specific narrow-tip raster measurement                                                                | [log](logs/webkit-browser.log), [JSON](data/webkit-browser.json)                                           |\n| CV PDF build                                     | Pass: all 120 PDFs, page limits and readable text layers                                                                    | [log](logs/cv.log)                                                                                         |\n\nThe initial Firefox attempt failed because only Chromium was installed. The\nenvironment failure is preserved in [firefox-missing-browser.log](logs/firefox-missing-browser.log).\nInstalling the pinned Firefox and WebKit revisions fixed the environment;\nno application workaround or dependency change was required.\n\nThe browser suite checks exact SVG equality after applying automatic turns/gaps,\nsharing and reloading; it edits cards, removes and renumbers a link, and checks\nthat English/Russian controls stay within the phone viewport. Actual SVG paint\nis rasterized at 2000 × 2000 pixels with a two-pixel boundary tolerance,\nequivalent to one pixel in a 1000 × 1000 image. A bounded Linux WebKit probe\nconfirmed antialias quantization at the smaller resolution; the original\nfailure and pixel rows are retained in `webkit-1000px-reproduction.log` and\n`data/webkit-pixels.json`. No application change was needed. It independently checks miter joins and\npainted boundary alignment at 5°, 15° and 45°. Full pixel measurements and SVGs\nare preserved in each engine's JSON, alongside screenshots. Zero page errors\nare required.\n\nThe local issue 23 compatibility run uses its default two gallery batches\n(1215 cards) to respect the container's 2.92 GiB shared memory limit. CI retains\nthe pre-existing eight-batch **4131-card** check for each engine, including\nnative WebKit display capture on macOS. The full browser suites run sequentially;\nevery experiment closes its browser and server. No unbounded stress probe is used.\n\nA long combined validation command was interrupted by the command runner\nbefore its final unit summary; its partial output is preserved in\n[all-tests-interrupted.log](logs/all-tests-interrupted.log). The final unit\nrun uses a standalone background process and records its exit status in\n[unit-exit-code.txt](logs/unit-exit-code.txt). This separates execution-runner\nlimits from test failures.\n\n## CI provenance\n\nThe baseline run [40397527295](https://github.com/konard/konard.github.io/actions/runs/40397527295)\nwas created at 20:39:02 UTC for `a80408d` and passed. It must not be confused\nwith validation of the changes. See [completed metadata](data/baseline-ci-final.json)\nand [complete log](logs/baseline-ci.log).\n\nThe source-validation run is\n[40401691502](https://github.com/konard/konard.github.io/actions/runs/40401691502),\ncreated after the push at 21:07:39 UTC for `3d077c2`.\nIt completed successfully at 21:12 UTC: lint/actionlint, audit, 717 unit tests,\nall five browser suites on Chromium/Firefox/macOS WebKit, the production build\nand 120 CV PDFs passed. See [metadata](data/source-ci.json),\n[complete logs](logs/source-ci.log) and [artifact inventory](data/source-ci-artifacts.json).\nDownloaded browser JSON is preserved under `data/ci-source`, with all\nissue-specific CI screenshots under `screenshots/ci-source`. Complete browser\nartifacts remain linked in the run. The final evidence commit is checked by\nanother fresh run before the PR is marked ready; its URL and exact SHA are\nrecorded in the PR description, avoiding a self-referential archive commit loop.\n\n## Final review\n// Experimental (issue #17): fewer overlaps of the lines of a network. Each end\n// of a link may leave its source or enter its target at another angle (the\n// per-link turns of glyph.js). This tries turns for one end at a time and\n// keeps the one that makes the drawing cleaner, a few passes over every end\n// (coordinate descent). Only the turned link changes, so only its pairs with\n// the other links are measured again.\n//\n// Editor scoring includes painted shafts, markers, fills and requested space\n// between them, including near referenced middles. The original centerline\n// scoring remains available for legacy shapes whose clearance is null.\n// A small turn penalty discourages changing angles without a reason.\nimport { bezier, curveTransform, layout, layoutCurves, linkCurve, shapeOf, paintedCurve, curveMarkers } from './glyph';\nimport { trimCurve } from './curve-tools';\nimport { paintedPairCost, selfCost } from './painted-collisions';\nimport { adjustCollisionGaps } from './collision-gaps';\n\nconst SAMPLES = 16; // points per Bézier segment\nconst NEAR = 0.09; // lines closer than this overlap (a stroke is about 0.04)\nconst MIDDLE = 0.14; // touching around a middle is the drawing, not an overlap\nconst CROSSING = 1;\nconst CLOSE = 0.25;\nconst TURNING = 0.002; // per degree\n\nexport const polyline = (curve) =>\n  curve.segments.flatMap((seg, k) =>\n    Array.from({ length: SAMPLES + (k ? 0 : 1) }, (_, j) => bezier(seg, (j + (k ? 1 : 0)) / SAMPLES)),\n  );\n\nconst distance = (a, b) => Math.hypot(a[0] - b[0], a[1] - b[1]);\n\nfunction crossing(p1, p2, q1, q2) {\n  const d = (a, b, c) => (b[0] - a[0]) * (c[1] - a[1]) - (b[1] - a[1]) * (c[0] - a[0]);\n  const [d1, d2, d3, d4] = [d(q1, q2, p1), d(q1, q2, p2), d(p1, p2, q1), d(p1, p2, q2)];\n  if (!(d1 * d2 < 0 && d3 * d4 < 0)) return null;\n  const t = d1 / (d1 - d2);\n  return [p1[0] + t * (p2[0] - p1[0]), p1[1] + t * (p2[1] - p1[1])];\n}\n\n/** How much the lines of two links (polylines) overlap and cross; `middles` are exempt. */\nexport function pairCost(a, b, middles) {\n  if (a.width !== undefined || b.width !== undefined) return paintedPairCost(a, b);\n  const free = (p) => p && middles.every((m) => distance(p, m) > MIDDLE);\n  let cost = 0;\n  for (let i = 0; i < a.length - 1; i++) {\n    for (let j = 0; j < b.length - 1; j++) {\n      if (!a[i] || !a[i + 1] || !b[j] || !b[j + 1]) continue;\n      const point = crossing(a[i], a[i + 1], b[j], b[j + 1]);\n      if (point && free(point)) cost += CROSSING;\n    }\n  }\n  for (const p of a) {\n    if (!free(p)) continue;\n    if (b.some((q) => q && distance(p, q) < NEAR)) cost += CLOSE;\n  }\n  for (const q of b) {\n    if (!free(q)) continue;\n    if (a.some((p) => p && distance(p, q) < NEAR)) cost += CLOSE;\n  }\n  return cost;\n}\n\nconst turning = (turns) => turns.flat().reduce((sum, a) => sum + Math.abs(a), 0) * TURNING;\n\n/** The cost of a drawing of `links` with `shape` (lower is cleaner). */\nexport function overlapCost(links, shape = {}) {\n  const curves = layoutCurves(links, shape);\n  const o = shapeOf(shape);\n  const scale = curveTransform(curves, o).scale;\n  const lines = curves.map((curve, i) => visiblePolyline(curve, o, i, scale));\n  const middles = curves.map((c) => c.middle.at);\n  let cost = turning(shapeOf(shape).turns) + lines.reduce((sum, line) => sum + selfCost(line), 0);\n  for (let i = 0; i < lines.length; i++)\n    for (let j = i + 1; j < lines.length; j++) cost += pairCost(lines[i], lines[j], middles);\n  return cost;\n}\n\n/**\n * Turns of the ends of every link that make the drawing cleaner. `shape.turns`\n * are kept as the starting point; the result adds turns from −range to +range\n * degrees in steps of `step`. Returns the turns found (`delta`, to add to the\n * starting turns), the turns in total (`turns`) and the cost before and after.\n */\nfunction solveTurns(links, shape = {}, { range = 60, step = 15, passes = 3 } = {}) {\n  range = Math.min(180, Math.max(0, Number(range) || 0));\n  step = Math.max(1, Number(step) || 15);\n  passes = Math.min(10, Math.max(0, Number(passes) || 0));\n  const n = links.length;\n  const base = shapeOf(shape);\n  const start = Array.from({ length: n }, (_, i) => base.turns[i] || [0, 0]);\n  const delta = start.map(() => [0, 0]);\n  const total = () => start.map((pair, i) => [pair[0] + delta[i][0], pair[1] + delta[i][1]]);\n  const places = layout(n, base, links);\n  const curveOf = (i) => linkCurve(links, i, places, { ...base, turns: total() });\n  const middles = layoutCurves(links, base).map((c) => c.middle.at);\n  const scale = curveTransform(layoutCurves(links, base), base).scale;\n  const lines = links.map((_, i) => visiblePolyline(curveOf(i), base, i, scale));\n  const costOf = (i, line) => {\n    let cost = selfCost(line);\n    for (let j = 0; j < n; j++) if (j !== i) cost += pairCost(line, lines[j], middles);\n    return cost + turning([total()[i]]);\n  };\n  const before = overlapCost(links, base);\n  const candidates = [0];\n  for (let a = step; a <= range; a += step) candidates.push(a, -a);\n\n  for (let pass = 0; pass < passes; pass++) {\n    let improved = false;\n    for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n      for (let end = 0; end < 2; end++) {\n        // A self-closed half is already positioned; move the open references.\n        if (links[i][end] === i + 1) continue;\n        const kept = delta[i][end];\n        let best = { angle: kept, cost: costOf(i, lines[i]), line: lines[i] };\n        for (const angle of candidates) {\n          if (angle === kept) continue;\n          // Applied turns go back through the editable table's −180…180° range.\n          if (Math.abs(start[i][end] + angle) > 180) continue;\n          delta[i][end] = angle;\n          const line = visiblePolyline(curveOf(i), base, i, scale);\n          const cost = costOf(i, line);\n          if (cost < best.cost - 1e-9) best = { angle, cost, line };\n        }\n        delta[i][end] = best.angle;\n        lines[i] = best.line;\n        if (best.angle !== kept) improved = true;\n      }\n    }\n    if (!improved) break;\n  }\n  let result = {\n    delta,\n    turns: total(),\n    linkGaps: base.linkGaps,\n    before,\n    after: overlapCost(links, { ...base, turns: total() }),\n  };\n  // Middle cuts use image units: a turn can change fitting scale. Reject a\n  // cached candidate if the exact complete drawing would become worse.\n  if (result.after > before)\n    result = { delta: start.map(() => [0, 0]), turns: start, linkGaps: base.linkGaps, before, after: before };\n\n  return result;\n}\n\n/** Gap-first search avoids the angle-only local minimum at collapsed\n * reference ends. Turn the separated drawing, then refine the gaps again.\n * Every stage returns an exact refitted score and preserves the user's bounds.\n */\nexport function solveCollisions(links, shape = {}, options = {}) {\n  const { adjustGaps = false, gapRange = 0.2, middleRange = 4, passes = 3, debug = false } = options;\n  const base = shapeOf(shape);\n  let result;\n  if (adjustGaps) {\n    const turns = links.map((_, i) => base.turns[i] || [0, 0]);\n    const before = overlapCost(links, base);\n    const initial = { turns, delta: turns.map(() => [0, 0]), linkGaps: base.linkGaps, before, after: before };\n    const gaps = adjustCollisionGaps(links, base, initial, { gapRange, middleRange, passes });\n    result = solveTurns(links, { ...base, linkGaps: gaps.linkGaps }, options);\n    result.before = before;\n    result = adjustCollisionGaps(links, base, result, { gapRange, middleRange, passes });\nimport { useEffect, useLayoutEffect, useState } from 'react';\nimport { replaceAddress } from '../history';\n\n/** Opt-in tracing: localStorage.setItem('network.debug', 'true'). */\nexport function networkDebug(event, detail) {\n  try {\n    if (localStorage.getItem('network.debug') === 'true') console.debug(`[network] ${event}`, detail);\n  } catch {\n    // Storage can be unavailable in a private browser.\n  }\n}\n\nconst SLIDER_KEYS = ['ArrowLeft', 'ArrowRight', 'ArrowUp', 'ArrowDown', 'Home', 'End', 'PageUp', 'PageDown'];\nconst continuous = (target) => target?.matches?.('input[type=\"range\"], input[type=\"color\"]');\n\n/** Live state stays in React; history is a debounced, best-effort persistence layer. */\nexport function useNetworkHistory(query) {\n  const [interacting, setInteracting] = useState(false);\n  // Bind before paint: a first touch must not fall between mounting the input\n  // and installing passive effects (observable in mobile WebKit).\n  useLayoutEffect(() => {\n    const active = new Set();\n    let control = null;\n    const kind = (type) => (type.startsWith('pointer') ? 'pointer' : type.startsWith('touch') ? 'touch' : 'keyboard');\n    const start = (event) => {\n      if (continuous(event.target) && (event.type !== 'keydown' || SLIDER_KEYS.includes(event.key))) {\n        control = event.target;\n        active.add(kind(event.type));\n        networkDebug('interaction started', { type: event.type, control: event.target.id });\n        setInteracting(true);\n      }\n    };\n    const end = (event) => {\n      if (!active.size) return;\n      if (event.type === 'blur') active.clear();\n      else if (event.type === 'focusout') {\n        if (event.target !== control) return;\n        active.delete('keyboard');\n        if (control.type === 'color') active.clear();\n      } else {\n        if (event.type === 'keyup' && !SLIDER_KEYS.includes(event.key)) return;\n        if (event.type.startsWith('touch') && event.touches?.length) return;\n        active.delete(kind(event.type));\n      }\n      networkDebug('interaction ended', { type: event.type, remaining: [...active] });\n      setInteracting(active.size > 0);\n    };\n    const starts = ['pointerdown', 'touchstart', 'keydown'];\n    const ends = ['pointerup', 'pointercancel', 'touchend', 'touchcancel', 'keyup', 'focusout'];\n    starts.forEach((name) => document.addEventListener(name, start));\n    ends.forEach((name) => document.addEventListener(name, end));\n    window.addEventListener('blur', end);\n    return () => {\n      starts.forEach((name) => document.removeEventListener(name, start));\n      ends.forEach((name) => document.removeEventListener(name, end));\n      window.removeEventListener('blur', end);\n    };\n  }, []);\n\n  useEffect(() => {\n    if (interacting) return;\n    let timer;\n    let failures = 0;\n    const write = () => {\n      if (window.location.search === query) return;\n      const error = replaceAddress(`${window.location.pathname}${query}${window.location.hash}`);\n      if (error) {\n        networkDebug('address write failed', { name: error.name, message: error.message, failures });\n        // A rate-limited or temporarily inactive document must never take down the editor.\n        if (failures < 5) timer = setTimeout(write, 1000 * 2 ** failures++);\n      } else networkDebug('address saved', query);\n    };\n    timer = setTimeout(write, 400);\n    return () => clearTimeout(timer);\n  }, [query, interacting]);\n}\nKeyboard: setting-glass-edge\n[\n  \"historical URL upgrades through history, compacts default rows, and reloads the exact SVG\",\n  \"native rasterized closed gaps agree within 0.12 image units at 5°, 15°, 45°, 85°\",\n  \"automatic spacing preserves the closed link, changes open references, and applies/shares/reloads exactly\",\n  \"0.07↔0.08 arrows/native stepping, inherited decimal steps, negative typing, select-all, delete, Home and Tab\",\n  \"all 37 rendered network and 55 settings sliders support all eight navigation keys\"\n]\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
