[2026-10-27T20:10:45.866Z] [STDOUT] {"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_97","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json,datetime,shutil\nfrom pathlib import Path\nroot=Path('docs/case-studies/issue-27')\nresearch=[\n('https://www.w3.org/TR/SVG/painting.html#StrokeMiterlimitProperty','SVG 2 painting','Sharp miter geometry extends paint beyond a path vertex; cap geometry contributes to the actual painted endpoint. The application must compensate with a stable axis.'),\n('https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/input.html#number-state-(type=number)','HTML number input','Number controls use their value, step, minimum and step base. A placeholder is not the inherited numerical value. Native decimal stepping needs an explicit fractional step.'),\n('https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/input.html#dom-input-stepup','HTML stepping algorithms','Stepping an off-grid value snaps to a valid value in the chosen direction; the shared keyboard handler follows those semantics.'),\n('https://www.w3.org/WAI/ARIA/apg/patterns/slider/','WAI slider pattern','Arrow keys change one step, Home/End select bounds, and optional PageUp/PageDown supply larger steps.'),\n('https://www.w3.org/WAI/ARIA/apg/patterns/spinbutton/','WAI spinbutton pattern','Supports increment/decrement, optional larger increments and ordinary platform text editing. Native editable input text navigation remains available.'),\n('https://www.radix-ui.com/primitives/docs/components/slider','Radix Slider alternative','Custom slider supports step, bounds, keyboard navigation and controlled state. Useful for custom multi-thumb needs; adding it is unnecessary for this native input fix.'),\n('https://react-aria.adobe.com/NumberField','React Aria NumberField alternative','Provides number entry, stepper controls, bounds and localized numeric formatting. A candidate for a future localized input design; current native controls retain existing styling and semantics.')]\n(root/'data/research.json').write_text(json.dumps({'researchedAt':'2026-10-27','sources':[{'url':u,'title':t,'finding':f} for u,t,f in research],'method':'Official source pages browsed with web tools. Findings are paraphrases. The full HTML input page loaded during initial research; a later anchored fetch timed out.'},indent=2)+'\\\\n')\nfor name,target in [('issue27-all-tests.log','all-tests-first-pass.log'),('issue27-focused-final.log','focused-final.log'),('issue27-build-before.log','build-before.log'),('issue27-build-after.log','build-after.log'),('issue27-browser-chromium.log','browser-chromium-initial.log'),('issue27-browser-firefox.log','browser-firefox-initial.log'),('issue27-npm-ci.log','npm-ci.log'),('issue27-browsers-install.log','browser-install.log')]:\n src=Path('/tmp')/name\n if src.exists(): shutil.copyfile(src,root/'logs'/target)\np=root/'PLAN.md'\ns=p.read_text()\nfor line in s.splitlines():\n if line.startswith('- [ ]') and not any(word in line for word in ('Run complete local','Commit atomic','Fetch/merge','Re-read latest')):\n  s=s.replace(line,line.replace('[ ]','[x]'))\np.write_text(s)\nPY\ncat > docs/case-studies/issue-27/VALIDATION.md <<'EOF'\n# Validation record\n\nThe before state is prepared parent \"'`406a2b4`, containing the merged issue-25 implementation. Native browser checks use the pinned Playwright 1.63.0 browsers. All substantial commands write logs to files and run sequentially under the container'\"'s 2.92 GiB memory budget.\n\n## Reproduction and focused checks\n\n- Five initial geometry/solver/serialization tests fail before the fixes: [log](logs/reproduce-tests.log).\n- Three additional keyboard regressions fail: [log](logs/reproduce-keyboard-tests.log). The URL test was run after the serializer fix and already passed.\n- The new off-grid stepping check fails with \"'`0.075 → 0.085`: [log](logs/off-grid-reproduction.log). The same attempt records a fixture path error, corrected before acceptance.\n- All 19 new focused tests then pass: [log](logs/focused-final.log). They cover painted equality/continuity, exact manual arrangement, full/partial closed halves, all six historical schema revisions, old aliases and compact rows, URL history, inherited stepping, negative drafts and every slider schema.\n- Historical source audit passes all six schemas, retaining 53–84 fields as the schema grows: [audit log](logs/url-history-audit.log), [fixture](data/url-schema-history.json).\n\n## Full verification\n\nAn initial full suite passed **727 tests in 45 files** before the final nine historical-schema/shared-key regressions were added: [log](logs/all-tests-first-pass.log). Final local and CI results follow below after those commands complete.\n\nThe initial production Chromium and Firefox runs pass all five browser groups: preserved/canonical historical URLs, four rasterized arrow angles, automatic spacing/apply/share/reload, native and keyboard decimal stepping and editing, and all eight keys on 92 rendered sliders. Their [JSON data](data/) includes exact painted distances, browser versions, exercised control IDs and page errors. The final runs below use the completed off-grid stepping handler.\n\nThe final build retains the application'\"'s existing warnings about extensionless imports and bundle chunks. JSDOM emits its existing unsupported canvas warnings; the browser suites verify actual canvas rendering and downloads.\n\n## Verification boundaries\n\n- The solver remains an opt-in overlap heuristic. The exact symmetric manual arrangement is verified separately; default solving finds a zero-overlap arrangement with unequal open-lens gaps while preserving all self-closed halves.\n- Analytic paint equality uses the shaft cap and sharp miter tip. Native raster tests allow 0.12 SVG units for pixel/antialiasing differences at 2000-pixel resolution; they do not weaken analytic equality.\n- Keyboard tests use real desktop browser engines. Native operating-system dialogs, touch assistive technologies and every operating-system clipboard/undo convention are not independently emulated. Their standard key events remain unintercepted.\n- Historical URLs preserve explicit supported configurations and parser compatibility. Omitted defaults have always followed the current application; the historical URL scheme contains no release identifier.\n- The initial full suite and Chromium validation briefly overlapped in this container; the cgroup approached its memory ceiling but recorded **zero OOM events/kills**. Subsequent heavy validation is sequential. No deliberately unbounded stress probes are used.\nEOF\ncat /tmp/issue27-check-final.log | tail -n 25; tail -n 8 /tmp/issue27-all-tests-final.log\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
