[2026-10-27T20:24:04.067Z] [STDOUT] {"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_161","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc 'tail -n 6 docs/case-studies/issue-27/logs/browser-webkit-final.log; tail -n 6 docs/case-studies/issue-27/logs/compat-issue25-firefox.log; cat /tmp/issue27-pr-body.md'","aggregated_output":"  - import \"./fields\" without a file extension (src/settings/schema.sound.js:7:47). Add the file extension\n  - import \"../skins.frames\" without a file extension (src/settings/schema.skins.js:3:25). Add the file extension\n  - import \"./fields\" without a file extension (src/settings/schema.layers.js:8:54). Add the file extension\n  - import \"./fields\" without a file extension (src/settings/schema.skins.js:4:47). Add the file extension\n  - import \"./fields\" without a file extension (src/settings/schema.background.js:3:54). Add the file extension\nSet `VITE_CONFIG_NATIVE_IGNORE_WARNING=true` to suppress this warning.\n  \"auto: apply/share/reload preserves exact drawing and discovered gaps\",\n  \"auto-gaps: apply/share/reload preserves exact drawing and discovered gaps\",\n  \"native SVG rasterization: sharp acute tips and aligned painted boundaries at 5°, 15°, 45°\",\n  \"visible card fields, editing, inheritance, sharing and removal/renumbering\",\n  \"English/Russian mobile card controls fit without horizontal scrolling\"\n]\nFixes #27.\n\nEqual reference gaps on a self-closed link now have exactly equal painted extents. The arrow correction uses each closed endpoint's tangent, removing the sudden jump between `0.07` and `0.08`, while retaining issue 25's common painted boundary for a lens referencing another link.\n\nAutomatic spacing preserves turns, reference gaps and middle cuts on fully or partially self-closed halves and optimizes open references. Shared URLs omit default turn rows and trailing inherited gap columns, accept every historical URL schema, and replace the address with the compact equivalent on arrival. A shared numeric component preserves intermediate text and inherited values; all slider and number renderers support consistent decimal stepping and keyboard navigation.\n\n### Reproduction and verification\n\nOpen `/network/?code=1111&rotation=-90&turns=0+0%2C-15+15&gaps=0.08+0.08+%7E+%7E%2C0.18+0.18+%7E+%7E`. Before the fix, source/target painted closed gaps measured **4.15 / 5.45** SVG units; after, **4.15 / 4.15**. Changing only the target from `0.07` to `0.08` now moves it by the expected **0.60**, rather than **1.90** units. The exact manual arrangement is a regression fixture.\n\n- Geometry, full/partial closed-half solver, historical-schema, URL history and numeric editing regressions are included. Failed-before logs, raw numerical measurements and independent rasterized SVG checks are archived.\n- `npm run check`, **736 unit tests** and production build pass. `npm run test:network:issue27` runs in Chromium, Firefox and WebKit alongside all existing browser suites in CI, with screenshots and JSON artifacts.\n- The [case study](https://github.com/konard/konard.github.io/blob/issue-27-5cf85bfa2348/docs/case-studies/issue-27/README.md) inventories every requirement, reconstructs the timeline, audits all six historical URL schemas, explains the root causes and alternatives, and includes source data, prior-session logs and [validation evidence](https://github.com/konard/konard.github.io/blob/issue-27-5cf85bfa2348/docs/case-studies/issue-27/VALIDATION.md).\n\nThe solver remains an opt-in overlap heuristic: it preserves the closed link but can choose different open-link gaps/turns from the symmetric manual fixture. Its preview, applied result and shared reload are identical. No external dependency defect was identified in this issue.\n\n### Before / after\n\nEqual closed gaps, with the upper lens kept at equal `0.18 / 0.18`:\n\n| Before | After |\n| --- | --- |\n| ![Before: oversized closed arrow gap](https://github.com/konard/konard.github.io/blob/issue-27-5cf85bfa2348/docs/case-studies/issue-27/screenshots/before-equal.png?raw=true) | ![After: equal painted closed gaps](https://github.com/konard/konard.github.io/blob/issue-27-5cf85bfa2348/docs/case-studies/issue-27/screenshots/chromium-after-equal.png?raw=true) |\n\nAutomatic spacing now preserves the closed link:\n\n| Before | After |\n| --- | --- |\n| ![Before: solver opens the closed loop](https://github.com/konard/konard.github.io/blob/issue-27-5cf85bfa2348/docs/case-studies/issue-27/screenshots/before-auto.png?raw=true) | ![After: solver adjusts open references](https://github.com/konard/konard.github.io/blob/issue-27-5cf85bfa2348/docs/case-studies/issue-27/screenshots/chromium-after-auto.png?raw=true) |\n\n![Final editor with per-link gap controls](https://github.com/konard/konard.github.io/blob/issue-27-5cf85bfa2348/docs/case-studies/issue-27/screenshots/chromium-after-editor.png?raw=true)\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
