[2026-10-27T20:55:28.822Z] [STDOUT] {"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/konard/konard.github.io/issues/27","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/konard/konard.github.io","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/konard/konard.github.io/issues/27/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/konard/konard.github.io/issues/27/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/konard/konard.github.io/issues/27/events","html_url":"https://github.com/konard/konard.github.io/issues/27","id":6066476924,"node_id":"I_kwDON1sLX88AAAABaZcXfA","number":27,"title":"Default gaps are still not perfect enough","user":{"login":"konard","id":1431904,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MzE5MDQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1431904?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard","html_url":"https://github.com/konard","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":8113453895,"node_id":"LA_kwDON1sLX88AAAAB45l7Rw","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/konard/konard.github.io/labels/bug","name":"bug","color":"d73a4a","default":true,"description":"Something isn't working","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":8113453898,"node_id":"LA_kwDON1sLX88AAAAB45l7Sg","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/konard/konard.github.io/labels/documentation","name":"documentation","color":"0075ca","default":true,"description":"Improvements or additions to documentation","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":8113453904,"node_id":"LA_kwDON1sLX88AAAAB45l7UA","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/konard/konard.github.io/labels/enhancement","name":"enhancement","color":"a2eeef","default":true,"description":"New feature or request","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":0,"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:45:26Z","updated_at":"2026-10-27T19:49:39Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"OWNER","active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"<img width=\"1824\" height=\"1112\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/cd7dc1bf-19db-4cd5-a334-4bbc9b25bb60\" />\n<img width=\"1824\" height=\"1112\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/07c18fb4-ce65-462b-bda6-6424dc0dfe15\" />\n\nThis is the link where I got it to the closest to perfect https://konard.github.io/network/?code=1111&rotation=-90&turns=0+0%2C-15+15&gaps=0.08+0.07+%7E+%7E%2C0.18+0.18+%7E+%7E Yet looks like 0.07 is still to close as a reference and 0.08 id too much of a gap. Rotation can be ignored for tests, and it works as expected. `turns=0+0%2C-15+15` that looks strange, do we not have 0 as defaults? Do we need to enter zerors? May be we can use some delimeter to just skip first item to make url shorter.\n\nAlso double check across our history of url changes and we do support all previous urls configuraton as I gave some public links to them, so backward compatibility must be preserved, and if we have a shorter version of the url it should be updated when user comes to the page (with write to history of browser).\n\nBy default `Gap at the target reference` results in much bigger gap on fully closed self referencing link, meaning 0.08 makes too much of a gap, yet 0.07 is closer to perfection, yet by default they must be exactly the same (must be tested and measured).\n\nSomething is wrong with switching between 0.07 and 0.08 of this setting, there is sudden jump, yet between 0.00 and 0.07 no such sudden jumps.\n\nAlso up/down buttons of this configurator should not reset the value to zero (i mean up/down should go in steps of 0.01, not 1, for some reason there is UI bug, I clicked on up or down and got zero instead of 0.07).\n\nAlso on all sliders and also input fields with numbers we need to double check keyboard arrows work, and double check for all other obvious and intuitive keyboard keys and short cuts are supported.\n\nAlso experiemental automatic gap in this case didn't end up at this configuration, may it is because we don't set preority to not break fully self closing ling by default. So if link is fully self closed most likely it is already at perfect position or partially closed (the closed part of it is already perfect). By default we should prioritize to changing gaps and angles in this experimental feature for other open ended links.\n\nAnd this exact perfect arrangement should be added to tests.\n\nLast time we did nice work at https://github.com/konard/konard.github.io/issues/25 on making 0.18 and 0.18 for upper link to land on exactly the same line, but the closed links was not perfected enough or broken.\n\nWe need to download all logs and data related about the issue to this repository, make sure we compile that data to `./docs/case-studies/issue-{id}` folder, and use it to do deep case study analysis (also make sure to search online for additional facts and data), in which we will reconstruct timeline/sequence of events, list of each and all requirements from the issue, find root causes of the each problem, and propose possible solutions and solution plans for each requirement (we should also check known existing components/libraries, that solve similar problem or can help in solutions).\n\nIf there is not enough data to find actual root cause, add debug output and verbose mode if not present, that will allow us to find root cause on next iteration.\n\nIf issue related to any other repository/project, where we can report issues on GitHub, please do so. Each issue must contain reproducible examples, workarounds and suggestions for fix the issue in code. Also double check to fully apply requirements to entire codebase, so if we have issue in multiple places, it should be fixed in all them.\n\nPlease plan and execute everything in this single pull request, you have unlimited time and context, as context auto-compacts and you can continue indefinitely, until it is each and every requirement fully addressed, and everything is totally done.","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/konard/konard.github.io/issues/27/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/konard/konard.github.io/issues/27/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null}[[]]{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/konard/konard.github.io/pulls/28","id":5040175487,"node_id":"PR_kwDON1sLX88AAAABLGr5fw","html_url":"https://github.com/konard/konard.github.io/pull/28","diff_url":"https://github.com/konard/konard.github.io/pull/28.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/konard/konard.github.io/pull/28.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/konard/konard.github.io/issues/28","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/konard/konard.github.io/pulls/28/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/konard/konard.github.io/pulls/28/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/konard/konard.github.io/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/konard/konard.github.io/issues/28/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/konard/konard.github.io/statuses/cdf…519","number":28,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"Fix closed-link gaps, preserve self loops and compact shared URLs","user":{"login":"konard","id":1431904,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MzE5MDQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1431904?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard","html_url":"https://github.com/konard","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Fixes #27.\n\nEqual reference gaps on a self-closed link now have exactly equal painted extents. The arrow correction uses each closed endpoint's tangent, removing the sudden jump between `0.07` and `0.08`, while retaining issue 25's common painted boundary for a lens referencing another link.\n\nAutomatic spacing preserves turns, reference gaps and middle cuts on fully or partially self-closed halves and optimizes open references. Shared URLs omit default turn rows and trailing inherited gap columns, accept every historical URL schema, and replace the address with the compact equivalent on arrival. A shared numeric component preserves intermediate text and inherited values, including native spinner clicks on empty inherited fields; all slider and number renderers support consistent decimal stepping and keyboard navigation.\n\n### Reproduction and verification\n\nOpen `/network/?code=1111&rotation=-90&turns=0+0%2C-15+15&gaps=0.08+0.08+%7E+%7E%2C0.18+0.18+%7E+%7E`. Before the fix, source/target painted closed gaps measured **4.15 / 5.45** SVG units; after, **4.15 / 4.15**. Changing only the target from `0.07` to `0.08` now moves it by the expected **0.60**, rather than **1.90** units. The exact manual arrangement is a regression fixture.\n\n- Geometry, full/partial closed-half solver, historical-schema, URL history and numeric editing regressions are included. Failed-before logs, raw numerical measurements and independent rasterized SVG checks are archived.\n- `npm run check`, **737 unit tests** and production build pass. `npm run test:network:issue27` runs in Chromium, Firefox and WebKit alongside all existing browser suites in CI, with screenshots and JSON artifacts. Playwright MCP verifies actual native spinner Up/Down clicks, including inherited values.\n- The [case study](https://github.com/konard/konard.github.io/blob/cdf…519/docs/case-studies/issue-27/README.md) inventories every requirement, reconstructs the timeline, audits all six historical URL schemas, explains the root causes and alternatives, and includes source data, prior-session logs and [validation evidence](https://github.com/konard/konard.github.io/blob/cdf…519/docs/case-studies/issue-27/VALIDATION.md).\n\nThe solver remains an opt-in overlap heuristic: it preserves the closed link but can choose different open-link gaps/turns from the symmetric manual fixture. Its preview, applied result and shared reload are identical. No external dependency defect was identified in this issue.\n\n### Before / after\n\nEqual closed gaps, with the upper lens kept at equal `0.18 / 0.18`:\n\n| Before | After |\n| --- | --- |\n| ![Before: oversized closed arrow gap](https://github.com/konard/konard.github.io/blob/cdf…519/docs/case-studies/issue-27/screenshots/before-equal.png?raw=true) | ![After: equal painted closed gaps](https://github.com/konard/konard.github.io/blob/cdf…519/docs/case-studies/issue-27/screenshots/chromium-after-equal.png?raw=true) |\n\nAutomatic spacing now preserves the closed link:\n\n| Before | After |\n| --- | --- |\n| ![Before: solver opens the closed loop](https://github.com/konard/konard.github.io/blob/cdf…519/docs/case-studies/issue-27/screenshots/before-auto.png?raw=true) | ![After: solver adjusts open references](https://github.com/konard/konard.github.io/blob/cdf…519/docs/case-studies/issue-27/screenshots/chromium-after-auto.png?raw=true) |\n\n![Final editor with per-link gap controls](https://github.com/konard/konard.github.io/blob/cdf…519/docs/case-studies/issue-27/screenshots/chromium-after-editor.png?raw=true)\n\n### Final CI\n\n[Run 40581017634](https://github.com/konard/konard.github.io/actions/runs/40581017634) passed on final commit `cdf…519`: all 737 unit tests, Chromium/Firefox/WebKit browser regressions, lint/format/audit, production build and 120 CV PDFs. Deployment is skipped for pull requests.\n","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:52:13Z","updated_at":"2026-10-27T20:55:22Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"44e2eb85e5a6001dc159ed3ec0ae67dbfbe8923b","assignee":{"login":"konard","id":1431904,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MzE5MDQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1431904?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard","html_url":"https://github.com/konard","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/received_events","type":"